# Stowed to ~/.stow-global-ignore.
#
# Stow checks a package's .stow-local-ignore first, then this file, and uses
# whichever it finds FIRST - it does not merge them with the built-in defaults
# (Stow.pm: get_ignore_regexps). So this file must restate those defaults, or
# they are silently lost.
#
# Everything above the last section is stow 2.4.1's built-in list, verbatim.

RCS
.+,v

CVS
\.\#.+       # CVS conflict files / emacs lock files
\.cvsignore

\.svn
_darcs
\.hg

\.git
\.gitignore
\.gitmodules

.+~          # emacs backup files
\#.*\#       # emacs autosave files

^/README.*
^/LICENSE.*
^/COPYING

# --- local additions ---

# Every package carries its own install.sh, which is run by install_all.sh and
# must never be symlinked into $HOME. _safely_stow passes --ignore for this,
# but a bare `stow <pkg>` does not - which is how ~/install.sh once appeared.
# Anchored so a genuinely nested install.sh inside a config tree still stows.
^/install\.sh$
